  "evidences": [
    {
      "id": "ev_1",
      "evidence_type": "report_text",
      "report_id": "TrendMicro_IXESHE_IHEATE(05-27-2016)",
      "locator": {
        "page": 1,
        "section": "body",
        "sentence_id": "p1_s1"
      },
      "text": "blog.trendmicro.com /trendlabs-security-intelligence/ixeshe-derivative-iheate-targets-users-america/ Since 2012, we’ve been keeping an eye on the IXESHE targeted attack campaign .",
      "language": "en",
      "confidence": 0.95,
      "note": "narrative sentence evidence",
      "source": "document"
    },
    {
      "id": "ev_5",
      "evidence_type": "report_text",
      "report_id": "TrendMicro_IXESHE_IHEATE(05-27-2016)",
      "locator": {
        "page": 1,
        "section": "body",
        "sentence_id": "p1_s5"
      },
      "text": "While there were some incremental improvements in the observed behavior of the new sample, the underlying pattern of behavior is similar to what we observed earlier from IXESHE.",
      "language": "en",
      "confidence": 0.95,
      "note": "narrative sentence evidence",
      "source": "document"
    },
    {
      "id": "ev_10",
      "evidence_type": "report_text",
      "report_id": "TrendMicro_IXESHE_IHEATE(05-27-2016)",
      "locator": {
        "page": 1,
        "section": "body",
        "sentence_id": "p1_s10"
      },
      "text": "IXESHE is a well-known targeted attack campaign which has mainly targeted East Asian governments, electronics manufacturers, and a telecommunications company in Germany.",
      "language": "en",
      "confidence": 0.95,
      "note": "narrative sentence evidence",
      "source": "document"
    },
    {
      "id": "ev_13",
      "evidence_type": "report_text",
      "report_id": "TrendMicro_IXESHE_IHEATE(05-27-2016)",
      "locator": {
        "page": 1,
        "section": "body",
        "sentence_id": "p1_s13"
      },
      "text": "Unlike common IXESHE variants which usually communicate with C&C servers via HTTP and a customized Base64-ecoded payload, IHEATE communicates with C&C servers in the TCP layer.",
      "language": "en",
      "confidence": 0.95,
      "note": "narrative sentence evidence",
      "source": "document"
    },
    {
      "id": "ev_16",
      "evidence_type": "report_text",
      "report_id": "TrendMicro_IXESHE_IHEATE(05-27-2016)",
      "locator": {
        "page": 2,
        "section": "body",
        "sentence_id": "p2_s1"
      },
      "text": "The threat actors behind IHEATE could use these tags to manage victims.",
      "language": "en",
      "confidence": 0.95,
      "note": "narrative sentence evidence",
      "source": "document"
    },
    {
      "id": "ev_23",
      "evidence_type": "report_text",
      "report_id": "TrendMicro_IXESHE_IHEATE(05-27-2016)",
      "locator": {
        "page": 3,
        "section": "body",
        "sentence_id": "p3_s4"
      },
      "text": "The client encrypts the session key using RSA-1024, using a public key hardcoded inside of malware.",
      "language": "en",
      "confidence": 0.95,
      "note": "narrative sentence evidence",
      "source": "document"
    },
    {
      "id": "ev_24",
      "evidence_type": "report_text",
      "report_id": "TrendMicro_IXESHE_IHEATE(05-27-2016)",
      "locator": {
        "page": 3,
        "section": "body",
        "sentence_id": "p3_s5"
      },
      "text": "File properties The IHEATE sample with the “EMC112” identiﬁer passes itself oﬀ as legitimate Media Player-related .DLL ﬁle, as can be seen below:",
      "language": "en",
      "confidence": 0.95,
      "note": "narrative sentence evidence",
      "source": "document"
    },
    {
      "id": "ev_25",
      "evidence_type": "report_text",
      "report_id": "TrendMicro_IXESHE_IHEATE(05-27-2016)",
      "locator": {
        "page": 4,
        "section": "body",
        "sentence_id": "p4_s1"
      },
      "text": "The IHEATE sample with the “EMC112” identiﬁer used the subdomain cknew[.]{abused domain}[.]com as the location of its C&C server.",
      "language": "en",
      "confidence": 0.95,
      "note": "narrative sentence evidence",
      "source": "document"
    },
    {
      "id": "ev_28",
      "evidence_type": "report_text",
      "report_id": "TrendMicro_IXESHE_IHEATE(05-27-2016)",
      "locator": {
        "page": 5,
        "section": "body",
        "sentence_id": "p5_s1"
      },
      "text": "Other domains used by IHEATE also overlapped with servers used by IXESHE.",
      "language": "en",
      "confidence": 0.95,
      "note": "narrative sentence evidence",
      "source": "document"
    },
    {
      "id": "ev_29",
      "evidence_type": "report_text",
      "report_id": "TrendMicro_IXESHE_IHEATE(05-27-2016)",
      "locator": {
        "page": 5,
        "section": "body",
        "sentence_id": "p5_s2"
      },
      "text": "Two domains ( ipv6pro[.]root[.]sx and gimeover[.]psp-moscow[.]com ) were used by IHEATE and resolved to the IP address 200[.]93[.]193[.]163 .",
      "language": "en",
      "confidence": 0.95,
      "note": "narrative sentence evidence",
      "source": "document"
    },
    {
      "id": "ev_30",
      "evidence_type": "report_text",
      "report_id": "TrendMicro_IXESHE_IHEATE(05-27-2016)",
      "locator": {
        "page": 5,
        "section": "body",
        "sentence_id": "p5_s3"
      },
      "text": "At approximately the same time, IXESHE also used the same server – except it did so by accessing the domain skype[.]silksky[.]com .",
      "language": "en",
      "confidence": 0.95,
      "note": "narrative sentence evidence",
      "source": "document"
    },
    {
      "id": "ev_34",
      "evidence_type": "report_text",
      "report_id": "TrendMicro_IXESHE_IHEATE(05-27-2016)",
      "locator": {
        "page": 2,
